{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788470415-NVqX8TH9xcfYx6CaGSh1","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the full picture. The change needed is in `PlanningStep.to_messages` in `/testbed/src/smolagents/memory.py`:\n\nCurrently:\n```python\ndef to_messages(self, summary_mode: bool, **kwargs) -> List[Message]:\n    if summary_mode:\n        return []\n    return [Message(role=MessageRole.ASSISTANT, content=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": self.plan.strip()}])]\n```\n\nThe user wants: after the assistant plan message, append a user-style message \"Now go on and execute this plan.\" — exactly once after each plan, only when not in summary mode.\n\nSo the new behavior:\n```python\ndef to_messages(self, summary_mode: bool, **kwargs) -> List[Message]:\n    if summary_mode:\n        return []\n    return [\n        Message(role=MessageRole.ASSISTANT, content=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": self.plan.strip()}]),\n        Message(role=MessageRole.USER, content=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Now go on and execute this plan.\"}]),\n    ]\n```\n\nThis satisfies:\n- \"after the assistant displays the plan content\" — appended right after the ASSISTANT plan message\n- \"a user-style message\" — role USER\n- \"exactly once after each plan\" — `to_messages` is called once per planning step whenever memory is written to messages, so it appears exactly once per PlanningStep\n- \"only when the full conversation is being displayed (not in summary mode)\" — inside the `if summary_mode: return []` branch\n\nLet me also check the gradio_ui.py to see if plans are displayed there and whether the user-style message would show up in the UI. The user said \"the system to immediately show a user-style message\" — in the context of the conversation display. Let me check gradio_ui.py to see how PlanningStep is rendered.\n\nAlso let me check the memory.py `replay` method — there's a bug there: `step.facts + \"\\n\" +