{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788470633-u28iKmw95E92s32ZcHqE","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. When a plan enters the conversation, it's now automatically followed by a user-style message telling the assistant to execute it.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`src/smolagents/memory.py:152`** — `PlanningStep.to_messages()` now emits two messages instead of one:\n1. The plan as an `ASSISTANT` message (unchanged)\n2. `\"Now go on and execute this plan.\"` as a `USER` message, immediately after\n\n**`tests/test_memory.py`** — updated `test_planning_step_to_messages` to assert the follow-up's role, position, and exact text, and added `test_planning_step_to_messages_summary_mode` covering the summary-mode path.\n\n## How this meets each requirement\n\n| Requirement | How it's satisfied |\n|---|---|\n| Immediately after the plan | Appended as the very next message in the list returned per planning step |\n| User-style message | `MessageRole.USER` |\n| Exactly once per plan | `to_messages()` is called once per `PlanningStep` each time the conversation is built — one follow-up per plan, never duplicated. Verified with two plans in memory: 2 follow-ups, each directly after its own plan |\n| Only in full-conversation mode | The existing `if summary_mode: return []` guard covers both the plan and the follow-up — summary mode produces nothing |\n| Automatic and consistent | It's built into the step itself, so every plan gets it with no call-site changes — `write_memory_to_messages()` (used for model input and replays) picks it up everywhere |\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tests/test_memory.py`: **10 passed**\n- Full related suites (`test_agents.py`, `test_gradio_ui.py`, `test_monitoring.py`, `test_final_answer.py`): **83 passed** — nothing else depended on the old message count\n- End-to-end through `AgentMemory`: full mode shows `[system] → [assistant] Plan A → [user] execute → [assistant] Plan B → [user] execute`; summary mode shows zero messages from planning steps\n\nOne note: the Gradio streaming UI (`gradio_ui.py:130-134`) renders planning steps directly from `step_log.plan` rather than through `to_messages()`, so the on-screen chat bubble layout there is unchanged — the follow-up appears in the conversation sent to the model and in memory replays. If you'd also like a visible bubble in the Gradio chat, that's a small separate addition; let me know.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cf87932-3e90-459c-96d7-d0872a40be7e","uuid":"b99cd156-eba3-4a9d-8ddf-5eab2d716fac","timestamp":"2026-09-03T21:23:59.551Z","request_id":"gen-1788470633-u28iKmw95E92s32ZcHqE"}
